# Foundry system — always publish releases

When this workspace (`CTS-DND-35`) has **any change** that ships in the system zip (anything under `module/`, `templates/`, `css/`, `lang/`, `packs/`, `assets/`, or `system.json`), **finish by publishing**:

1. Bump `"version"` and `"download"` in `system.json` to the next patch (or minor if appropriate), matching tag `v{version}`.
2. Commit all release-related files with a clear message.
3. `git push origin main`
4. `git tag v{version}` and `git push origin v{version}` — this triggers `.github/workflows/release.yml`.

Do **not** leave fixes only on local `main` without a tag; the maintainer tests from GitHub releases / manifest.

Skip a new tag only for commits that **cannot** affect the installed system (e.g. README-only or `.github/` workflow edits only), unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.
